Algorithm:


Step 1: Start. Create an empty circular doubly linked list (head = NULL), an array of 10 free beds and an empty circular queue (size 5).
Step 2: Display the menu: admit, discharge, search, display forward, display backward, bed status, undo discharge, history, exit.
Step 3: Read the choice and call the matching function. Repeat Steps 2 and 3 until choice = 0.
Step 4: Admit: Find the first free bed in the array. If none is free, display "No beds available" and stop.
Step 5: Read patient ID. If the ID already exists in the list, display "Patient ID already exists" and stop.
Step 6: Read name, age and disease. Allot the bed number, mark the bed as occupied and increase count.
Step 7: Create a new node and insert it at the end of the list (tail = head->prev). Link tail->next = new node, new node->prev = tail, new node->next = head and head->prev = new node.
Step 8: Discharge: Read patient ID and search the list from head until the head is reached again. If not found, display "Patient not found" and stop.
Step 9: If the queue is full, remove (dequeue) the oldest record. Then insert (enqueue) the patient record at rear = (rear + 1) % size.
Step 10: Free the patient's bed in the array. Delete the node by linking its previous and next nodes (update head if the head is deleted), then decrease count.
Step 11: Search: Read the patient ID and traverse the list from head using next until head is reached again. If a node matches, display the patient details; otherwise display "Patient not found".
Step 12: Display forward: Start at head and print each node using next until head is reached again.
Step 13: Display backward: Start at tail (head->prev) and print each node using prev until tail is reached again.
Step 14: Bed status: Traverse the bed array and print each bed as free or occupied, along with the free bed count.
Step 15: Undo discharge: If the queue is empty, display a message and stop. Otherwise take the front (oldest) record, check that its ID is unused and that a free bed exists, then dequeue it (front = (front + 1) % size), allot a free bed and insert the patient at the end of the list.
Step 16: History: Print the queue records from front to rear (oldest discharge first). On exit, free all nodes and Stop.